{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TSfmtKgde5LDY7yd8wSGrb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd098-pinky\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/pinky: Lightweight Finger Information Lookup\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS does not ship pinky. GNU pinky is a lightweight alternative to finger that shows\n6\t  user information from the utmpx database and passwd entries. The Go implementation must\n7\t  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gpinky, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte,\n8\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Display logged-in user information in short or long format.\n12\t  - G2: Show GECOS field information (real name, office, phone) from passwd entries.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gpinky via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Short format (default)\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: Must display logged-in users in short format by default, showing login name, terminal, idle time, login time, and remote host, one line per user.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: When given USER arguments, must show information only for those users (from passwd and utmpx).\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"-s must force short format output (default behavior).\"\n25\t\n26\t  R2:\n27\t    title: Long format and field control\n28\t    items:\n29\t      - R2.1:\n30\t          text: \"-l must display long format output showing login name, real name (from GECOS), terminal, idle time, login time, office location, and office phone from the passwd entry.\"\n31\t      - R2.2:\n32\t          text: \"-f must suppress the header line in short format.\"\n33\t      - R2.3:\n34\t          text: \"-b must suppress the home directory and shell in long format. -h must suppress the project file. -p must suppress the plan file.\"\n35\t\n36\t  R3:\n37\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n38\t    items:\n39\t      - R3.1:\n40\t          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n41\t      - R3.2:\n42\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n43\t      - R3.3:\n44\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n45\t\n46\tnon_goals:\n47\t  - cmd/pinky does not read .plan or .project files from user home directories on macOS (unlike full finger).\n48\t\n49\tacceptance_criteria:\n50\t  - id: AC1\n51\t    criterion: \"pinky prints logged-in users in short format, matching gpinky.\"\n52\t    traces:\n53\t      - R1.1\n54\t  - id: AC2\n55\t    criterion: \"pinky -l user prints long format with GECOS info, matching gpinky -l.\"\n56\t    traces:\n57\t      - R2.1\n58\t  - id: AC3\n59\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gpinky passes.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R1.1\n62\t      - R2.1\n63\t  - id: AC4\n64\t    criterion: \"cmd/pinky compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n65\t    traces:\n66\t      - R1.1\n67\t      - R1.2\n68\t      - R1.3\n69\t      - R2.1\n70\t      - R2.2\n71\t      - R2.3\n72\t      - R3.1\n73\t      - R3.2\n74\t      - R3.3\n75\t\n76\tpackage_contract:\n77\t  imports:\n78\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c9000e-53af-4ec1-8c8c-b97ecd6c8f52","uuid":"439c869d-4bf8-4d91-a97f-d56fb1cde8bf","timestamp":"2026-05-24T04:16:28.507Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5574/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd098-pinky.yaml","content":"id: srd098-pinky\ntitle: \"cmd/pinky: Lightweight Finger Information Lookup\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS does not ship pinky. GNU pinky is a lightweight alternative to finger that shows\n  user information from the utmpx database and passwd entries. The Go implementation must\n  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gpinky, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte,\n  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Display logged-in user information in short or long format.\n  - G2: Show GECOS field information (real name, office, phone) from passwd entries.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gpinky via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Short format (default)\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must display logged-in users in short format by default, showing login name, terminal, idle time, login time, and remote host, one line per user.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When given USER arguments, must show information only for those users (from passwd and utmpx).\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-s must force short format output (default behavior).\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Long format and field control\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-l must display long format output showing login name, real name (from GECOS), terminal, idle time, login time, office location, and office phone from the passwd entry.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-f must suppress the header line in short format.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-b must suppress the home directory and shell in long format. -h must suppress the project file. -p must suppress the plan file.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/pinky does not read .plan or .project files from user home directories on macOS (unlike full finger).\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"pinky prints logged-in users in short format, matching gpinky.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"pinky -l user prints long format with GECOS info, matching gpinky -l.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gpinky passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/pinky compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":79,"startLine":1,"totalLines":79}}}
