{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) assigned task #5574: implement cmd/pinky error handling and differential tests for srd098-pinky requirements R3.1 (exit 0 on success), R3.2 (exit 1 on error), and R3.3 (SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler). The task requires modifying `cmd/pinky/main.go` to ensure proper error handling paths and creating `cmd/pinky/pinky_test.go` with differential tests comparing output against the `gpinky` Homebrew reference binary. Acceptance criteria include: tests pass or skip gracefully, go vet passes, differential tests cover core functionality/formatting/error cases, and all three R3.x requirements are implemented.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - CGo integration for utmpx database access (`#include <utmpx.h>`, `#include <pwd.h>`)\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs GNU reference\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Exit code contracts: 0 on success, 1 on any error\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gpinky\")` with `t.Skip` fallback for missing reference binary\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for compiling the Go binary under test\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for deterministic output comparison\n   - utmpx-based user information display (login name, terminal, idle time, login time, host)\n   - GECOS field parsing from passwd entries (name, office, phone)\n   - Short format (default, table with header) vs long format (`-l`, multi-line per user)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd098-pinky.yaml`\n     - Full SRD defining all requirements for the pinky utility\n     - R3.1: \"Must exit 0 on success\"\n     - R3.2: \"Must exit 1 on an