uld fail with invalid option errors. For the long format tests, I'll need to handle getting the current username from the environment. Rather than trying to predict exact output matches beforehand, I'll just write the test structure and let the differential testing framework reveal any mismatches between the two implementations.\n\nWriting test structure... Adding test cases... I'm running the test suite to compare the output between our implementation and the reference binary, but I'm noticing an issue with how error messages are being normalized. When the `-l` flag is used without a username, both binaries produce slightly different error messages with their respective binary names embedded in them. The normalizer needs to handle this properly so that both \"gpinky\" and \"pinky\" get converted to the same canonical form for comparison purposes. The regex pattern handles full paths like `/opt/homebrew/bin/gpinky` correctly, and I'm verifying it works across different error cases — unrecognized options, invalid short options, and help messages all normalize properly so both outputs match after applying the pattern.\n\nFor the long format test, I should just run it and see what happens since both binaries read from the same system database, so the output should be identical if the formatting is correct. The differential test will catch any subtle differences in timestamps or idle times that might occur between runs. in milliseconds, this is extremely unlikely. For timestamps of past login events stored in utmpx, those won't change between runs, so they'll match exactly. I'll write the test file now without adding idle time normalizers unless the tests actually fail due to timing issues. One thing I should check: whether our code and gpinky format user data the same way, particularly field widths. Looking at the error messages for the `-l` flag with no user specified, both binaries output similar messages after normalizing the binary name, so that should be fine.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the `-f -s` flag combination and how our code processes them independently, then I need to verify how gpinky handles nonexistent users with the `-l` flag—whether it errors or displays \"???\" like ours does.\n\nLet me check the error messages when no username is specified with `-l`. Both gpinky and our implementation should produce the same error, just with different binary names.\n\nNow I'm ready to write the test file. I need to be careful about how the Name column works—both implementations pull the first comma-separated field from GECOS, so those should align. I'm planning out the test cases to cover the main scenarios: default short format, the `-f` flag for no header, explicit `-s` flag, filtering by user, long format with `-l`, and variations with `-b`, `-h`, and `-p` flags.\n\nI also need to verify edge cases like what happens when `-l` is used without a username or with a nonexistent user—whether it exits with code 0 or 1, and make sure our implementation matches gpinky's behavior. I'm checking how the header formatting works with the `-f` flag to suppress it, and realizing that `-s` just sets the default short format which is already the default behavior. Now I need to write the test file, and I'll need to get the current user via environment variable for the long format tests, though I should handle the case where it's not set.\n\nWriting test file... Adding test cases...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1561,"cache_read_input_tokens":31686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1561},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c9000e-53af-4ec1-8c8c-b97ecd6c8f52","uuid":"0137da2d-08a6-460b-92e9-5e1b5c17924b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YGgjLwS1g6Xx1wXVVuiRJ5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011HPQCtMiqkFAz99Vy4thaF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5574/cmd/pinky/pinky_test.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Implements srd098-pinky R3.1, R3.2, R3.3.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gpinky\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n\t}\n\n\tbinaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?pinky`)\n\tnormalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n\t\treturn binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"pinky\"))\n\t})\n\terrNorm := []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName}\n\n\tuser := os.Getenv(\"USER\")\n\tif user == \"\" {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"USER environment variable not set\")\n\t}\n\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t{Name: \"no_args\", ExitCode: 0},\n\t\t{Name: \"short_no_header\", Args: []string{\"-f\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n\t\t{Name: \"explicit_short\", Args: []string{\"-s\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n\t\t{Name: \"short_with_user\", Args: []string{user}, ExitCode: 0},\n\t\t{Name: \"long_format\", Args: []string{\"-l\", user}, ExitCode: 0},\n\t\t{Name: \"long_no_home_shell\", Args: []string{\"-lb\", user}, ExitCode: 0},\n\t\t{Name: \"long_suppress_all\", Args: []string{\"-lbhp\", user}, ExitCode: 0},\n\t\t{Name: \"long_no_user\", Args: []string{\"-l\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n\t\t{Name: \"unrecognized_option\", Args: []string{\"--foo\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n\t\t{Name: \"invalid_short_option\", Args: []string{\"-x\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n\t}\n\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1561,"cache_read_input_tokens":31686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1561},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c9000e-53af-4ec1-8c8c-b97ecd6c8f52","uuid":"a50513a9-9e6b-4bf1-8050-0d5e0f27df1b"}
